meta {
  name: Two subjects in one period is not a clash
  type: http
  seq: 56
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/timetables/{{timetableId}}/slots
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  X-School-Id: {{schoolCode}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "section_id": "{{sectionId}}",
    "period_id": "{{periodOneId}}",
    "day_of_week": 1,
    "subject_offering_id": "{{electiveOfferingId}}"
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
  res.body.period_id: eq {{periodOneId}}
}

script:post-response {
  bru.setEnvVar("concurrentSlotId", res.body.id);
}

docs {
  THE CLASH UNIT IS THE STUDENT SET, NOT THE SECTION. This is a second class
  for the same section in the same period on the same day and it is accepted,
  because Grade XI runs Physics, History and Commerce concurrently and a pupil
  attends exactly one of them. Refusing on section would make a real school's
  timetable unrepresentable.

  It is accepted here specifically because no pupil is actively enrolled in
  both offerings by the time this folder runs - folder 05 drops the elective
  enrolment. Put one pupil in both and the same request answers 409 with rule
  "student_set", naming the pupils in the overlap.

  No room and no teacher are named, deliberately. A room here would collide
  with request 61, which moves maths into the laboratory in this period, and a
  teacher would collide with request 57.
}
